   "name": "L'atelier de réparation · The Repair Workshop",
   "room_id": "R_adj_state_02",
   "image": "reparation/reparation.jpg",
   "alt": "An open timber repair shed inside the glass-roofed market hall, seen from above. Round one small workbench an old repairman polishes a blue-dotted Polish mug beside a big white teapot still in one piece, a boy steadies a teetering stack of china plates, a girl pours golden glue into a pot and another girl holds up a clean butterfly net. On the bench a toy train runs round its figure-eight track, a jar is crammed with buttons, a neat porcelain swan sits beside a steaming kettle and a dripping dish towel, and a tangle of springs and gears lies in front. Below, a feather duster puffs dust off an old book, a worn-out boot stands under the bench, and an iron and a little broom wait. A red door and an archway to the market square are at the left; a blue door and a green door, with a bicycle between them, are at the right.",
