   "backTo": "reparation",
   "alt": "A small repair counter in a plank-walled shed under the glass roof, seen at eye level in warm lamplight. A young repairwoman paints the last shiny fins on a toy fish under a desk lamp clamped to the counter; a boy studies a pocket watch through a magnifying glass; a girl rings a red bell; a casserole dish lies cracked in two beside a bendy soup ladle and a full gumball machine. Above, a white eagle with a bandaged wing flies among a mobile of paper birds. In front, a chair holds a coat and a prize rosette, its leg tied up with wire; sand pours out of an empty dolls' house; a taped-up umbrella leans on the counter. A red door at the left leads back to the workshop.",
